  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Boosting Renewable Innovation for Green and Inclusive Transition (BRIGHT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indonesia has committed to achieving Net Zero Emissions by 2060 or earlier, with interim targets of 23% renewableenergy by 2025 and 31% by 2050. Yet progress remains slow: renewables make up less than 15% of the energy mix,and solar power&#x2014;despite its vast potential&#x2014;contributes only marginally. Closing this gap requires a dual approach:unlocking large-scale financing for the transition while ensuring renewable energy reaches communities that remain underserved.</narrative>
  </description>
